  - transition state
  - optimization
  - Rust
abstract: >-
  rgsaddle finds saddle points on a potential energy surface, the
  transition states between two minima. It is a Rust library with a C
  interface and a Python package, and its main searches are: a nudged
  elastic band (NEB) between two endpoints, with a climbing image; a
  minimum-mode search from one point, by the dimer method or by Lanczos
  iteration; an index-1 search on a dense Hessian by restricted-step
  partitioned rational function optimization (RFO).
